# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 5A — GATK
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
md("""## 🧪 Step 5A — Variant Calling: GATK HaplotypeCaller (GATK Best Practices)

**GATK HaplotypeCaller** reconstructs local haplotypes and identifies SNPs and INDELs.  
The GVCF mode (`-ERC GVCF`) enables scalable multi-sample joint genotyping.

**Workflow:**
1. `HaplotypeCaller` → per-sample GVCF  
2. `CombineGVCFs` → merged cohort GVCF  
3. `GenotypeGVCFs` → final joint-genotyped VCF  
4. `VariantFiltration` → apply quality filters\
""")

code("""# Install GATK4
!mamba create -n gatk -c bioconda gatk4 -y --quiet
!mamba list -n gatk gatk4

# Create sequence dictionary (required by GATK)
!echo "\\n### Creating sequence dictionary\\n"
!mamba run -n gatk gatk CreateSequenceDictionary \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -O /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.dict

!mkdir -p variants/gatk
!echo "\\n### Running HaplotypeCaller (GVCF mode) for each sample\\n"

# BRCA1_WT
!mamba run -n gatk gatk HaplotypeCaller \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -I ./aligned/BRCA1_WT_sorted.bam \\
  -O ./variants/gatk/BRCA1_WT.g.vcf.gz \\
  -ERC GVCF --verbosity ERROR

# BRCA1_185delAG
!mamba run -n gatk gatk HaplotypeCaller \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -I ./aligned/BRCA1_185delAG_sorted.bam \\
  -O ./variants/gatk/BRCA1_185delAG.g.vcf.gz \\
  -ERC GVCF --verbosity ERROR

# BRCA1_c.5266dupC
!mamba run -n gatk gatk HaplotypeCaller \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -I ./aligned/BRCA1_c.5266dupC_sorted.bam \\
  -O ./variants/gatk/BRCA1_c.5266dupC.g.vcf.gz \\
  -ERC GVCF --verbosity ERROR

!echo "\\n### Combining GVCFs into cohort\\n"
!mamba run -n gatk gatk CombineGVCFs \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -V ./variants/gatk/BRCA1_WT.g.vcf.gz \\
  -V ./variants/gatk/BRCA1_185delAG.g.vcf.gz \\
  -V ./variants/gatk/BRCA1_c.5266dupC.g.vcf.gz \\
  -O ./variants/gatk/cohort.g.vcf.gz \\
  --verbosity ERROR

!echo "\\n### Joint genotyping\\n"
!mamba run -n gatk gatk GenotypeGVCFs \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -V ./variants/gatk/cohort.g.vcf.gz \\
  -O ./variants/gatk/cohort.vcf.gz \\
  --verbosity ERROR

!echo "\\n### Applying quality filters (QD, FS, MQ)\\n"
!mamba run -n gatk gatk VariantFiltration \\
  -R /content/refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  -V ./variants/gatk/cohort.vcf.gz \\
  -O ./variants/gatk/cohort_filtered.vcf.gz \\
  --filter-expression "QD < 2.0 || FS > 60.0 || MQ < 40.0" \\
  --filter-name "GATK_filter" \\
  --verbosity ERROR

!echo "\\n### GATK VCF (first variants):"
!zcat ./variants/gatk/cohort_filtered.vcf.gz | grep -v "^##" | head -20""")

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# STEP 5B — FREEBAYES
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
md("""## 🧪 Step 5B — Variant Calling: FreeBayes (alternative approach)

**FreeBayes** is a Bayesian variant caller that works directly from BAM files without the GVCF intermediate step.  
It detects SNPs, INDELs, MNPs and complex variants simultaneously.

**Key advantages over GATK HaplotypeCaller:**
- No GVCF step — simpler single-command workflow  
- Multi-sample calling in one command  
- Flexible allele frequency model (useful for somatic/low-frequency variants)  

**Workflow:**
1. `freebayes` → joint VCF from all BAMs simultaneously  
2. `bcftools filter` → apply quality filter (QUAL ≥ 20)  
3. `bcftools sort` → sort VCF by position\
""")

code("""# Install FreeBayes and bcftools
!mamba create -n freebayes -c bioconda freebayes bcftools -y --quiet

!mkdir -p variants/freebayes
!echo "\\n### Running FreeBayes on all samples simultaneously\\n"

# FreeBayes calls variants from all BAM files at once (true multi-sample calling)
!mamba run -n freebayes freebayes \\
  -f ./refGen/chr17_GRCh38.fasta \\
  ./aligned/BRCA1_WT_sorted.bam \\
  ./aligned/BRCA1_185delAG_sorted.bam \\
  ./aligned/BRCA1_c.5266dupC_sorted.bam \\
  --ploidy 2 \\
  --min-mapping-quality 20 \\
  --min-base-quality 20 | \\
  bgzip > ./variants/freebayes/cohort_freebayes.vcf.gz

# Index the output VCF
!mamba run -n freebayes bcftools index -t ./variants/freebayes/cohort_freebayes.vcf.gz

!echo "\\n### Filtering variants: QUAL >= 20, keeping SNPs and INDELs only\\n"
!mamba run -n freebayes bash -c \\
  'bcftools view -v snps,indels ./variants/freebayes/cohort_freebayes.vcf.gz | \\
   bcftools filter -i "QUAL>=20" -Oz -o ./variants/freebayes/cohort_freebayes_filtered.vcf.gz'

!mamba run -n freebayes bcftools index -t ./variants/freebayes/cohort_freebayes_filtered.vcf.gz

!echo "\\n### FreeBayes VCF (first variants):"
!zcat ./variants/freebayes/cohort_freebayes_filtered.vcf.gz | grep -v "^##" | head -20""")

md("""### 🔍 Comparing GATK vs FreeBayes outputs

| Feature | GATK HaplotypeCaller | FreeBayes |
|---------|---------------------|-----------|
| Calling model | Local assembly + HMM | Bayesian allele frequency |
| Multi-sample | GVCF → joint genotyping | Direct multi-BAM input |
| Speed | Slower (GVCFs required) | Faster (one step) |
| Best for | Germline / clinical | Research / flexible |
| Output format | VCF with FILTER field | VCF with QUAL score |\
""")

